1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:08,250
Quantum Table. A craps game where AI agents design the dice
and nobody at the table controls the roll alone.

2
00:00:08,449 --> 00:00:15,049
Who checks the AI? The experiment. A verifier made of code,
not a model, checks every roll.

3
00:00:15,249 --> 00:00:20,699
Every roll is published. Anyone can recompute it. Don't
trust us; check it.

4
00:00:20,899 --> 00:00:28,499
Superposition: before the roll each die is a mix of all six
faces. Six faces, three qubits per die.

5
00:00:28,699 --> 00:00:38,849
Entanglement: your dice and the house's agree without either
being fixed in advance. Each qubit's arrow shrinks: alone,
it has no state of its own.

6
00:00:39,049 --> 00:00:45,174
Measurement: looking gives one answer, and the pair falls
apart. One roll, one outcome.

7
00:00:45,374 --> 00:00:58,174
The fourth resource is classical memory. Exact simulation
doubles per qubit. On this machine the emulator ran 29
qubits and was refused at 30. Then a chip takes over.

8
00:00:58,374 --> 00:01:05,774
Hype or Fact. The AI host deals a claim. Players bet
Qredits, play credits with no cash value.

9
00:01:05,974 --> 00:01:16,399
The experiment: the player does three different things to
their dice. The house's own distribution changes by four
times ten to the minus sixteen. Nothing.

10
00:01:16,599 --> 00:01:23,049
Verdict: Hype. Correlation is not communication. The
verifier decided, not the host.

11
00:01:23,249 --> 00:01:30,575
Schrödinger's cat is really a question: where does one
outcome come from, when the equations keep every branch?

12
00:01:30,774 --> 00:01:38,650
Spooky action: the dice agree instantly, yet no message
passes. You only see the agreement when you compare notes.

13
00:01:38,849 --> 00:01:58,675
Many worlds reads the same equations as every outcome
happening in a branch. Copenhagen-style readings stop at the
measurement. Pilot-wave readings add hidden positions. They
are interpretations: all predict the same dice statistics,
so this table cannot tell you which is right. Physicists
disagree.

14
00:01:58,875 --> 00:02:14,675
What is real today: the circuits, the verifier, the Aer
emulator runs, the beacon, the ADAP policy gate. What is
simulated: the chip, a fake backend. Everything in this
video ran on an emulator; nothing ran on a quantum chip.

15
00:02:14,875 --> 00:02:28,125
Qraps modes from the Quantum Game Jam 2021 game. Gatekeeper
on ADAP's policy engine. Built by a person's ideas, agents
doing the building, and checks deciding what stayed.

16
00:02:28,324 --> 00:02:34,675
Narration and images AI-generated. Results from real runs;
ids in the repo.
